Using type assertions in this way can be helpful when dealing with values that may have multiple possible types in theory, but you know for certain that they will only have one specific type in practice. However, it's important to use type assertions sparingly and only when you have a clear understanding of the implications. Type assertions can be helpful, but they can also lead to potential bugs if used incorrectly.

